# Line endings, settled in one place.
#
# Every tracked file in this repository is text: ~3,700 markdown documents, the
# generator and gate scripts, and the JSON they emit. There is not one binary
# asset, which is why this file can afford to be blunt.
#
# THE INCIDENT. Until 2026-08-28 this repository had no `.gitattributes`, and the
# machine holding the primary checkout carried a system-level `core.autocrlf=true`
# under a repository-level `core.autocrlf=false`. So the tree was checked out CRLF
# and then normalisation was switched off for writes: every file sat CRLF on disk
# against an LF index. Git hides that as long as nobody touches a file - the stat
# cache marks it clean - and reveals it the moment anybody does.
#
# The cost was not cosmetic. It fell on REVIEW, which is the one job in this
# repository that cannot be delegated:
#
#   - A worker's four-file edit first presented as 514 insertions / 466 deletions
#     instead of 58 / 8.
#   - One landed commit changed 61 real lines in a document and reported 682 -
#     91% of that diff was carriage returns.
#   - Two prose files conflicted across their ENTIRE length on a routine merge
#     (line 1 to line 420) when their true difference was five lines.
#
# A reviewer who cannot see the change cannot judge it, and a corpus whose whole
# governance model is "a human reads the diff before it is adopted" cannot afford
# an instrument that hides diffs. `check-hash-stability.mjs` had been asserting the
# generated output is byte-identical across LF and CRLF checkouts all along - that
# gate is about the PRODUCT of the scripts, and it stayed green while the SOURCE
# rotted underneath it. A green gate over the wrong population, one more time.
#
# THE RULE. `text=auto eol=lf` - normalise on the way into the index, and check out
# LF as well, so disk and index agree and no future contributor's `core.autocrlf`
# can reintroduce the divergence. The whole tree was renormalised in one commit
# beside this file; that commit is mechanical and touches everything, which is why
# it stands alone and is labelled as such.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Belt and braces for the future: this repository holds no binary assets today, so
# any that arrive would otherwise be caught by the blanket rule above and corrupted.
*.png  binary
*.jpg  binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif  binary
*.webp binary
*.ico  binary
*.pdf  binary
*.zip  binary
*.woff  binary
*.woff2 binary
*.mp4  binary
*.mp3  binary
*.wav  binary
